# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
import lib/cadkernel/brep_bounds.dl
import lib/cadkernel/brep_make.dl

function bounds3 point {a 64 bit floating-point number array of 3 items:values}:
    execute:
        return a cad vector3 with x (the item at 0 in values), y (the item at 1 in values) and z (the item at 2 in values)
function check bounds3 {boolean:condition}:
    execute:
        if condition = false:
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "abort", nothing)
function check bounds3 point {cad vector3:point} near {cad vector3:expected}:
    execute:
        check bounds3 ((the cad distance from point to expected) < 1e-12)

set points to a list containing (bounds3 point [1.0,-2.0,3.0])
append (bounds3 point [-4.0,5.0,-6.0]) to points
append (the cad zero vector3) to points
set bounded to the cad box around points
check bounds3 (bounded's valid)
check bounds3 point (bounded's value's low) near (bounds3 point [-4.0,-2.0,-6.0])
check bounds3 point (bounded's value's high) near (bounds3 point [1.0,5.0,3.0])
loop index from 0 to the length of points:
    check bounds3 ((bounded's value) holds cad point (the item at index in points))
free points
set empty to an empty list of a cad vector3
set absent to the cad box around empty
check bounds3 ((absent's valid) = false)
free empty
print "a_box_around_points_holds_every_one_of_them" as a line

set one to a cad box3 from (the cad zero vector3) to (bounds3 point [1.0,1.0,1.0])
set touching to a cad box3 from (bounds3 point [1.0,0.0,0.0]) to (bounds3 point [2.0,1.0,1.0])
set apart to a cad box3 from (bounds3 point [2.0,0.0,0.0]) to (bounds3 point [3.0,1.0,1.0])
check bounds3 (one overlaps cad box touching)
check bounds3 ((one overlaps cad box apart) = false)
check bounds3 ((the cad separation of one and touching) = 0.0)
check bounds3 ((the absolute value of ((the cad separation of one and apart) - 1.0)) < 1e-12)
print "boxes_that_touch_overlap_and_boxes_apart_do_not" as a line

set justPast to a cad box3 from (bounds3 point [1.0000001,0.0,0.0]) to (bounds3 point [2.0,1.0,1.0])
check bounds3 ((one overlaps cad box justPast) = false)
check bounds3 ((the cad box one grown by 1e-6) overlaps cad box justPast)
print "padding_lets_a_touching_pair_through" as a line

set made to the cad cuboid at (bounds3 point [1.0,2.0,3.0]) with size (bounds3 point [4.0,5.0,6.0])
check bounds3 (made's valid)
set bounded to the cad bounds of (made's value)
check bounds3 (bounded's valid)
check bounds3 point (bounded's value's low) near (bounds3 point [1.0,2.0,3.0])
check bounds3 point (bounded's value's high) near (bounds3 point [5.0,7.0,9.0])
check bounds3 point (the cad size of (bounded's value)) near (bounds3 point [4.0,5.0,6.0])
check bounds3 point (the cad centre of (bounded's value)) near (bounds3 point [3.0,4.5,6.0])
print "a_box_bounds_its_own_faces" as a line

set faces to the cad face keys of (made's value)
loop index from 0 to the length of faces:
    set faceBounds to the cad bounds of (the item at index in faces) in (made's value)
    check bounds3 (faceBounds's valid)
    set size to the cad size of (faceBounds's value)
    set flat to 0
    if (size's x) < 1e-12:
        increment flat
    if (size's y) < 1e-12:
        increment flat
    if (size's z) < 1e-12:
        increment flat
    check bounds3 (flat = 1)
free faces
print "each_face_of_a_box_is_flat_in_one_direction" as a line

set survey to the cad cuboid at (bounds3 point [512345.678,4512345.678,91.5]) with size (bounds3 point [0.001,0.002,0.003])
check bounds3 (survey's valid)
set bounded to the cad bounds of (survey's value)
check bounds3 (bounded's valid)
set size to the cad size of (bounded's value)
check bounds3 ((the absolute value of ((size's x) - 0.001)) < 1e-9)
check bounds3 ((the absolute value of ((size's z) - 0.003)) < 1e-9)
print "survey_coordinates_bound_without_losing_the_size" as a line

set distant to a cad box3 from (bounds3 point [1e308,0.0,0.0]) to (bounds3 point [1.5e308,0.0,0.0])
set centre to the cad centre of distant
check bounds3 ((the absolute value of (centre's x)) <= 1.7976931348623157e308)
check bounds3 (distant holds cad point centre)
print "the_centre_of_a_distant_box_is_between_its_corners" as a line
